  "name": "CYTOCHROME P450 2D6 GENOTYPING (CYP2D6 - ALLELES)",
  "code": "2319",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<ul data-start=\"856\" data-end=\"1359\">\n<li data-start=\"856\" data-end=\"980\">\n<p data-start=\"858\" data-end=\"980\"><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\"><strong data-start=\"858\" data-end=\"868\">CYP2D6</strong> is involved in metabolism of ~25% of commonly used drugs including antidepressants, opioids, and beta-blockers.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 9px;\" data-start=\"981\" data-end=\"1359\">\n<p data-start=\"983\" data-end=\"1041\"><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\"><strong data-start=\"983\" data-end=\"995\">Genotype</strong> is used to classify drug metabolism capacity:</span></p>\n<ul data-start=\"1044\" data-end=\"1359\">\n<li style=\"font-size: 9px;\" data-start=\"1044\" data-end=\"1122\">\n<p data-start=\"1046\" data-end=\"1122\"><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\"><strong data-start=\"1046\" data-end=\"1072\">Poor Metabolizer (PM):</strong> &darr; enzyme activity &ndash; higher risk of drug toxicity.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 9px;\" data-start=\"1125\" data-end=\"1197\">\n<p data-start=\"1127\" data-end=\"1197\"><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\"><strong data-start=\"1127\" data-end=\"1161\">Intermediate Metabolizer (IM):</strong> Moderately reduced enzyme activity.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 9px;\" data-start=\"1200\" data-end=\"1250\">\n<p data-start=\"1202\" data-end=\"1250\"><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\"><strong data-start=\"1202\" data-end=\"1233\">Extensive Metabolizer (EM):</strong> Normal activity.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 9px;\" data-start=\"1253\" data-end=\"1359\">\n<p data-start=\"1255\" data-end=\"1359\"><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\"><strong data-start=\"1255\" data-end=\"1288\">Ultra-Rapid Metabolizer (UM):</strong> &uarr; enzyme activity &ndash; risk of therapeutic failure due to fast clearance.</span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 data-start=\"1366\" data-end=\"1394\"><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\"><strong data-start=\"1373\" data-end=\"1394\">Clinical Utility:</strong></span></h3>\n<ul data-start=\"1396\" data-end=\"1629\">\n<li style=\"font-size: 9px;\" data-start=\"1396\" data-end=\"1486\">\n<p data-start=\"1398\" data-end=\"1486\"><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\">Helps <strong data-start=\"1404\" data-end=\"1434\">individualize drug therapy</strong> (e.g., codeine, tamoxifen, fluoxetine, metoprolol).</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 9px;\" data-start=\"1487\" data-end=\"1556\">\n<p data-start=\"1489\" data-end=\"1556\"><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\">Reduces risk of <strong data-start=\"1505\" data-end=\"1531\">adverse drug reactions</strong> and <strong data-start=\"1536\" data-end=\"1555\">drug inefficacy</strong>.</span></p>\n</li>\n<li style=\"font-size: 9px;\" data-start=\"1557\" data-end=\"1629\">\n<p data-start=\"1559\" data-end=\"1629\"><span style=\"font-size: 9px;\">Used in <strong data-start=\"1567\" data-end=\"1587\">pharmacogenomics</strong> and <strong data-start=\"1592\" data-end=\"1617\">personalized medicine</strong> approaches.</span></p>\n</li>\n</ul>",
